WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.590 --> 00:00:07.960
In the opening scene where Elise tries to
contact the dead when she's in the bedroom

00:00:07.960 --> 00:00:11.760
with her brother, she ends up summoning a
demon who appears on the bed behind her for

00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:12.760
a fraction of a second.

00:00:12.760 --> 00:00:17.380
This appears to be a younger version of the
lipstick faced demon, who years later becomes

00:00:17.380 --> 00:00:21.780
the driving force behind the Lambert haunting
in the original Insidious.

00:00:21.780 --> 00:00:25.520
We also see a small horse figurine in the
room, which resembles the one found in Lipstick

00:00:25.520 --> 00:00:27.310
Face's lair in The Further.

00:00:27.310 --> 00:00:30.830
Horses may just be a recurring element in
The Further, as we see them in Parker Crane's

00:00:30.830 --> 00:00:31.830
room as well.

00:00:31.830 --> 00:00:35.980
Elise and Christian's room also have a toy
monkey, which we also see many of in Parker's

00:00:35.980 --> 00:00:36.980
room.

00:00:36.980 --> 00:00:41.130
I have a theory on how Elise may have allowed
the Lambert incident to begin due to her actions

00:00:41.130 --> 00:00:44.840
in the The Last Key, which I'll get back to
later on in this video.

00:00:44.840 --> 00:00:47.641
Elise's father is often seen plopped in front
of the TV.

00:00:47.641 --> 00:00:51.420
But if you pay attention to what he's watching,
it says a lot about his character.

00:00:51.420 --> 00:00:54.890
First he's seen watching a documentary about
Joseph Stalin and Marxism.

00:00:54.890 --> 00:00:59.510
I never paid much attention in history class,
but I do know that Stalin was a communist

00:00:59.510 --> 00:01:05.330
dictator back in the USSR and Marxism was
an ideology that was the basis for communism.

00:01:05.330 --> 00:01:09.870
If you think about it, his household is a
communist dictatorship, where he is the dictator.

00:01:09.870 --> 00:01:14.069
In fact, when he punishes Elise, the mother
begs him not to go hard on her, but he says,

00:01:14.069 --> 00:01:17.179
"don't tell me how to punish her, I punish
people for a living."

00:01:17.179 --> 00:01:21.420
He also forces Elise to to ignore her psychic
gift and lie about the existence of spirits

00:01:21.420 --> 00:01:25.649
in their house because she's the only one
with this ability and in communism, everything

00:01:25.649 --> 00:01:29.500
is controlled by the state, or in this case,
her father, and everyone's contribution must

00:01:29.500 --> 00:01:30.500
be equal.

00:01:30.500 --> 00:01:34.289
So he tries to force Elise to dumb herself
down so that she can't use this power that

00:01:34.289 --> 00:01:38.240
her brother doesn't have, which is a method
used by communist leaders to keep people in

00:01:38.240 --> 00:01:40.399
line and prevent an uprising.

00:01:40.399 --> 00:01:44.399
Another one of the programs he watches is
Duck and Cover which was a propaganda film

00:01:44.399 --> 00:01:46.450
shown to schoolchildren in the 1950s.

00:01:46.450 --> 00:01:50.759
It was supposed to teach them what to do if
a nuclear attack hits, but really it was created

00:01:50.759 --> 00:01:53.929
to give people a false sense of security as
not to raise panic.

00:01:53.929 --> 00:01:57.961
I mean, come on, this isn't Attack on Titan,
covering your neck would not actually save

00:01:57.961 --> 00:01:59.649
you if a bomb went off.

00:01:59.649 --> 00:02:04.399
But in many ways Gerald Rainier uses these
same tactics on his daughter by forcing Elise

00:02:04.399 --> 00:02:07.090
to ignore the presence of the demons in her
household.

00:02:07.090 --> 00:02:11.230
This way she stays quiet and doesn't create
hysteria with her brother and her mom when

00:02:11.230 --> 00:02:13.060
these presences are haunting them.

00:02:13.060 --> 00:02:16.980
And Gerald knows full-well that these demons
exist and knows of their power, because he's

00:02:16.980 --> 00:02:20.909
been manipulated by The Man With The Keys,
who forces him to keep these women locked

00:02:20.909 --> 00:02:21.909
in his basement.

00:02:21.909 --> 00:02:23.980
And let's have a closer look at this basement.

00:02:23.980 --> 00:02:28.459
It's filled with shelves of canned food, and
you can spot a gas mask hanging on the wall.

00:02:28.459 --> 00:02:33.049
Maybe this basement is not just a basement,
but also a fallout shelter, somewhere you

00:02:33.049 --> 00:02:36.459
might go to protect yourself from these communist
attacks.

00:02:36.459 --> 00:02:39.609
Something that probably works better than
Duck and Cover.

00:02:39.609 --> 00:02:42.870
This shelter is where Elise is put when she
defies her father's orders.

00:02:42.870 --> 00:02:46.430
The gas mask could also be a reference to
how Elise first learned to communicate with

00:02:46.430 --> 00:02:49.859
the beings from The Further, as we see here
in the first Insidious.

00:02:49.859 --> 00:02:54.480
When she goes back to the basement as an adult,
the calendar still reads September 1953, meaning

00:02:54.480 --> 00:02:58.170
her father never went back down there after
losing his wife.

00:02:58.170 --> 00:03:01.569
So the fallout shelter comes to represent
a resistance against communism.

00:03:01.569 --> 00:03:06.870
In fact, if you look back on major historical
events in September 1953, one of the biggest

00:03:06.870 --> 00:03:11.260
stories was communist China being rejected
from joining United Nations at the request

00:03:11.260 --> 00:03:14.299
of another communist nation, the Soviet Union.

00:03:14.299 --> 00:03:18.480
Plus, Gerald's prison warden jacket is very
reminiscent of something you might see on

00:03:18.480 --> 00:03:20.330
a Soviet general in World War II.

00:03:20.330 --> 00:03:24.280
There's a scene early on where we see the
silhouette of this jacket moving around behind

00:03:24.280 --> 00:03:28.629
Elise as she explores the basement, which
is an early clue that her father was involved

00:03:28.629 --> 00:03:31.459
with the supernatural entities that resided
there.

00:03:31.459 --> 00:03:36.519
The house is located at 414 Appletree Road
in Five Keys, New Mexico.

00:03:36.519 --> 00:03:40.280
As mentioned when I talked about the trailer,
it's a fictional location, so choices such

00:03:40.280 --> 00:03:43.360
as making this welcome sign look like a tombstone
are deliberate.

00:03:43.360 --> 00:03:46.440
It's kind of hinted that the whole town is
filled with malicious ghosts because of the

00:03:46.440 --> 00:03:50.999
executions that take place at the large prison
facility, which seems to be the main feature

00:03:50.999 --> 00:03:52.129
of Five Keys.

00:03:52.129 --> 00:03:55.680
One character tells Elise she is lucky to
have gotten out of the town; and her niece,

00:03:55.680 --> 00:04:00.530
Imogen claims to have also seen these spirits,
despite the fact that she never actually visited

00:04:00.530 --> 00:04:02.249
the house Elise grew up in.

00:04:02.249 --> 00:04:06.340
It seems like the whole town is plagued by
these occurrences and Elise's childhood home

00:04:06.340 --> 00:04:09.359
has the worst of it due to the close proximity
with the prison.

00:04:09.359 --> 00:04:13.590
The street address, 414 Appletree Road, could
be a reference to this being the fourth movie

00:04:13.590 --> 00:04:16.410
in the franchise and leading directly into
the first movie.

00:04:16.410 --> 00:04:20.310
Early on in The Last Key, Elise mentions that
she refuses to go back into The Further, after

00:04:20.310 --> 00:04:23.880
a close call while helping out Quinn Brenner,
which is a reference to her stand-off with

00:04:23.880 --> 00:04:26.320
The Black Bride in Insidious: Chapter 3.

00:04:26.320 --> 00:04:30.020
This explains why she will no longer astral
project, because she knows the Black Bride

00:04:30.020 --> 00:04:32.169
will be there waiting for her if she does.

00:04:32.169 --> 00:04:36.280
This is why she's unable to go into The Further
and guide Josh when he goes to retrieve Dalton

00:04:36.280 --> 00:04:37.470
in Insidious.

00:04:37.470 --> 00:04:41.110
In The Last Key, her mother is the one who
saves her from The Man With The Keys.

00:04:41.110 --> 00:04:45.610
The experience gives her a newfound respect
for her mother, so much so that she refuses

00:04:45.610 --> 00:04:47.780
to take ownership of her last name from that
point forward.

00:04:47.780 --> 00:04:48.780
"Please, call me Elise.

00:04:48.780 --> 00:04:51.009
Mrs. Rainier was my mother."

00:04:51.009 --> 00:04:55.030
It's also where she discovered that The Further
doesn't adhere to a linear flow of time.

00:04:55.030 --> 00:04:58.720
Elise meets and gives advice to a younger
version of herself in this movie, which would

00:04:58.720 --> 00:05:02.830
seem to be the first experience she has with
The Further bringing together timelines in

00:05:02.830 --> 00:05:03.830
the real world.

00:05:03.830 --> 00:05:08.759
There's evidence that she knows about this
in Insidious, "The Further is a world far

00:05:08.759 --> 00:05:11.840
beyond our own, yet it's all around us.

00:05:11.840 --> 00:05:16.591
A place without time as we know it," and it
plays a much bigger part in Chapter 2 when

00:05:16.591 --> 00:05:18.090
Josh does the same thing.

00:05:18.090 --> 00:05:22.520
He meets a younger version of himself to help
track down the location of The Black Bride.

00:05:22.520 --> 00:05:26.500
At the end of Insidious: Chapter 3, Elise
joins up with Specs and Tucker, but mentions

00:05:26.500 --> 00:05:29.919
that if they're going to go into business
together, they'll need to dress nicer.

00:05:29.919 --> 00:05:34.340
In this movie, Elise gives them the new clothes,
which they subsequently wear in Insidious

00:05:34.340 --> 00:05:37.270
and whenever they are on the job in Insidious
Chapter 2.

00:05:37.270 --> 00:05:40.449
Elise mentions that the clothes are some of
Jack's old outfits.

00:05:40.449 --> 00:05:44.500
Jack is her deceased husband whose image can
be seen in Chapter 3, when The Man Who Can't

00:05:44.500 --> 00:05:48.180
Breathe tries to trick her into taking her
life by pretending to be Jack.

00:05:48.180 --> 00:05:51.650
Sure enough, the outfit he's wearing in this
scene matches up with the outfits that Elise

00:05:51.650 --> 00:05:55.380
provides Specs and Tucker with, which become
part of their signature look in the series

00:05:55.380 --> 00:05:56.550
going forward.

00:05:56.550 --> 00:06:01.229
It's not entirely clear how much of Elise's
father's behaviour is just him being evil,

00:06:01.229 --> 00:06:04.620
and how much of it is due to him being controlled
by The Man With The Keys.

00:06:04.620 --> 00:06:08.580
But we do see evidence that the Key Man's
victims may have had some control at some

00:06:08.580 --> 00:06:09.580
point.

00:06:09.580 --> 00:06:13.720
When Elise returns to the house in 2010 after
Ted Garza has moved in, most of the interior

00:06:13.720 --> 00:06:18.659
decorations are the same, but Garza has added
some religious symbols: a cross on the wall

00:06:18.659 --> 00:06:23.000
and many copies of his Holy Bible, which he
expresses a belief that it will help Elise

00:06:23.000 --> 00:06:28.090
ward off the bad spirits, which seems more
like something out of The Exorcist than Insidious,

00:06:28.090 --> 00:06:29.860
which is why it doesn't really work.

00:06:29.860 --> 00:06:32.979
There's also a nod to another Exorcism movie
though.

00:06:32.979 --> 00:06:37.060
Elise's dog appears in both this film and
the previous film, and his name is Warren.

00:06:37.060 --> 00:06:41.861
Ed and Lorraine Warren are Elise's ghost-hunting
counterparts in The Conjuring franchise, the

00:06:41.861 --> 00:06:46.820
other big 4-film horror series started by
James Wan under the Blumhouse banner.

00:06:46.820 --> 00:06:49.539
Anna is the woman being kept prisoner in the
basement.

00:06:49.539 --> 00:06:53.760
When they find her, you may notice that she
has a considerable amount of leg hair, suggesting

00:06:53.760 --> 00:06:56.910
that she's been trapped down there for a very
long time.

00:06:56.910 --> 00:07:01.539
When Elise goes to investigate further, she
finds the suitcases of at least 4 other women

00:07:01.539 --> 00:07:02.939
who were taken prisoner down there.

00:07:02.939 --> 00:07:06.570
They each contain information about the person
and their skull.

00:07:06.570 --> 00:07:10.370
The one thing each victim has in common is
that they are all female nurses.

00:07:10.370 --> 00:07:14.590
It's never fully explained why this key demon
is only interested in nurses, but it does

00:07:14.590 --> 00:07:18.830
make me wonder if this is somehow connected
to Lorraine Lambert, Josh's mother.

00:07:18.830 --> 00:07:22.880
In Chapter 2, the Black Bride first encounters
Josh as a child when he is waiting for his

00:07:22.880 --> 00:07:26.220
mom to get off work at the hospital, as a
nurse.

00:07:26.220 --> 00:07:30.280
Parker Crane, who ends up being The Black
Bride, attacks Josh, and it's discovered that

00:07:30.280 --> 00:07:34.120
one day later, he jumped off the roof of the
hospital, killing himself.

00:07:34.120 --> 00:07:40.020
Lorraine finds this out after a creepy elevator
ride with Parker's ghost...

00:07:40.020 --> 00:07:41.370
"Parker?

00:07:41.370 --> 00:07:45.419
What are you?

00:07:45.419 --> 00:07:46.419
You should be resting, you shouldn't be out
of bed.

00:07:46.419 --> 00:07:47.419
Listen, I want to apologize for my son the
other day.

00:07:47.419 --> 00:07:49.020
He was being a nosy kid."

00:07:49.020 --> 00:07:52.189
Let me know your thoughts about the whole
nurse thing in the comments.

00:07:52.189 --> 00:07:56.710
Earlier I mentioned how I think Elise is responsible
for the Red Faced Demon getting to Dalton

00:07:56.710 --> 00:07:58.419
Lambert in the first movie.

00:07:58.419 --> 00:08:02.219
It starts with these red doors, which we learn
more about here in The Last Key.

00:08:02.219 --> 00:08:06.110
Elise mentions that previously she used a
red door to go deeper into The Further.

00:08:06.110 --> 00:08:09.360
She's talking about Quinn Brenner's apartment,
which is an interesting case, because the

00:08:09.360 --> 00:08:13.810
first time she passes through it, she's brought
to The Lambert's second house, which she hasn't

00:08:13.810 --> 00:08:14.840
even been to yet.

00:08:14.840 --> 00:08:18.199
The second time, under the guide of one of
the ghosts of the apartment, the same door

00:08:18.199 --> 00:08:22.860
takes her to the abandoned 5th floor of the
apartment complex, which is the home of The

00:08:22.860 --> 00:08:24.009
Man Who Can't Breathe.

00:08:24.009 --> 00:08:27.990
In Insidious, Josh passes through a red door
to get to The Lipstick Faced Demon's lair.

00:08:27.990 --> 00:08:32.530
And in Chapter 2, Josh, Elise and Carl pass
through a red door to get to Parker Crane's

00:08:32.530 --> 00:08:33.669
childhood room.

00:08:33.669 --> 00:08:37.270
In The Last Key, there is another red door,
and it leads to the penitentiary where The

00:08:37.270 --> 00:08:41.030
Man With The Keys lives, and this is where
the final showdown takes place.

00:08:41.030 --> 00:08:45.180
So based on the examples we have so far, it
looks like red doors typically lead to the

00:08:45.180 --> 00:08:47.600
lair of the demon who is haunting that area.

00:08:47.600 --> 00:08:51.590
However, it would appear that there are certain
cases where a red door will take someone to

00:08:51.590 --> 00:08:55.810
another time period, and we see it happen
one more time when Elise is on her way back

00:08:55.810 --> 00:08:57.970
to the real world in Chapter 4.

00:08:57.970 --> 00:09:02.060
She stumbles upon the first Lambert house,
and sees Dalton fall off the ladder.

00:09:02.060 --> 00:09:05.810
When she goes back through the door, she leaves
it open, and the darth maul looking demon

00:09:05.810 --> 00:09:09.610
who has been following her all these years
sees the chance to go after Dalton and try

00:09:09.610 --> 00:09:14.110
to take over his body to get back to the real
world, which was his objective all along.

00:09:14.110 --> 00:09:18.850
So in many ways, the key-fingered demon, despite
being defeated, still accomplished his goal.

00:09:18.850 --> 00:09:23.100
He has been trying to get Elise to open all
of these doors ever since she was a child

00:09:23.100 --> 00:09:26.300
and she opens the one that leads The Lipstick
Face demon to Dalton.

00:09:26.300 --> 00:09:29.960
The Man With The Keys leaves all these keys
around for Elise to open the doors, but at

00:09:29.960 --> 00:09:33.700
the end of day, the last key is Elise.

00:09:33.700 --> 00:09:37.370
So then the question becomes, why do these
doors keep leading Elise back to the Lambert

00:09:37.370 --> 00:09:38.370
family?

00:09:38.370 --> 00:09:41.630
It could be The Further, or someone in The
Further, such as Elise's mother, trying to

00:09:41.630 --> 00:09:45.200
show her that this is where she meets her
fate, and it is hinted at many times throughout

00:09:45.200 --> 00:09:46.200
the four films.

00:09:46.200 --> 00:09:49.460
But it doesn't do any good because The Black
Bride still ends up getting the better of

00:09:49.460 --> 00:09:53.520
Elise at the end of Insidious and the lipstick
faced demon is still on the loose at the end

00:09:53.520 --> 00:09:56.000
of the continuity that we've seen so far.

00:09:56.000 --> 00:10:00.690
So Leigh Whannell, if you're watching this,
it's been two movies since that cliffhanger,

00:10:00.690 --> 00:10:05.670
I think it's time in Chapter 5 to tie this
one up and give us a sequel to Chapter 2.

00:10:05.670 --> 00:10:09.450
Whenever that Chapter 5 trailer does drop,
you can bet I'll be covering it, until then

00:10:09.450 --> 00:10:14.250
remember to subscribe to CZsWorld for new
horrors every week, ring that deathbell for

00:10:14.250 --> 00:10:17.070
notifications and I'll see you in the next
one.

00:10:17.070 --> 00:10:18.910
Assuming we both survive.

